<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">State of Cauca</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1857–1886</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Sovereign State of Cauca</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The State of Cauca was a federal state of Colombia created in 1857 within the Granadine Confederation, covering a vast area of the south-west from the Pacific coast to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amazon">Amazon</a>, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/popayan">Popayán</a>. Its governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tomas-cipriano-de-mosquera">Tomás Cipriano de Mosquera</a> rebelled against the confederation in 1860 and won the civil war that followed. As the Sovereign State of Cauca it lasted until 1886.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/state-of-cauca.jpg" alt="State of Cauca" width="320" height="354" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Milenioscuro · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cauca_in_Granadine_Confederation.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
